---
Run a compact Apple M4 model-family health smoke with cache and receipt checks

Usage: bitnet mac smoke [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Configuration file path

      --model-family <MODEL_FAMILY>
          Model family to smoke. BitNet smoke uses one-shot ask; fixed warm proof is `mac bitnet-warm`

          Possible values:
          - dense-slm: Run the dense Qwen SLM golden smoke path
          - bitnet:    Run the explicit BitNet one-shot ask smoke path

          [default: dense-slm]

  -d, --device <DEVICE>
          Device/backend label (cpu, cuda/gpu, hip/rocm, oneapi, npu/openvino-npu, nvidia-rtx-5070-ti-cuda/wgpu, intel-a770-opencl, metal/mpsgraph, apple-m4-metal, apple-m4-mpsgraph, apple-m4-cpu-neon, apple-m3-air-metal, apple-m3-air-mpsgraph, apple-m3-air-cpu-neon, auto). Apple M4 and M3 Air labels are distinct proof lanes

      --model-id <MODEL_ID>
          Supported model id. Defaults to the validated Apple M4 SLM runtime artifact

          [default: qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0]

      --cache-dir <PATH>
          Override model cache root. Defaults to ~/.cache/bitnet-rs/models

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)

      --model-path <PATH>
          Explicit BitNet GGUF path. Only accepted with --model-family bitnet

      --batch-size <SIZE>
          Batch size for processing

      --tokenizer <PATH>
          Explicit BitNet tokenizer path. Only accepted with --model-family bitnet

      --max-new-tokens <MAX_NEW_TOKENS>
          Maximum new tokens for the fixed smoke prompt

          [default: 4]
          [aliases: --max-tokens, --n-predict]

      --threads <THREADS>
          Number of CPU threads to use (0 = all cores; deterministic mode may override)

          [default: 0]

      --json-out <PATH>
          Output aggregate golden smoke receipt

          [default: target/apple-m4-continuity/mac-smoke.json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
